# ADM-Cube Paper books: the pre-open order sheet of every SSE session, per book.
# Install or refresh with: /home/lzp/miniconda3/envs/quant/bin/python ops/cron/install_tushare_cron.py --block paper
#
# Books live in data/trading/paper/<book>/ (run_paper.py init). Each run goes
# through every book in turn: it settles the sessions whose data has been
# committed, decides today's session at its 08:30 inference time and writes
# logs/paper/<book>/<date>_orders.md plus that book's latest_orders.md. A book
# that cannot decide writes the reason to the same files and the run continues
# with the next book, exiting non-zero if any book failed. Weekday holidays
# exit at once.

SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
CRON_TZ=Asia/Shanghai
REPO_ROOT=/Data2/lzp/ADMCubeQuant
QUANT_PYTHON=/home/lzp/miniconda3/envs/quant/bin/python

# The operator declares the sheet's orders by hand: an at-open order goes into
# the 09:15-09:25 call auction, everything else from 09:30. The three runs
# therefore all have to land before 09:15.
#
# 05:40 is the first, after the nightly chain has committed the previous
# session: the evening update (23:35, visible from 03:05), the intraday-flow
# build (02:45), the PIT event build (03:35), the revision sentinel (04:00) and
# the text audit (05:00). Each book takes its PIT build, the replay of its
# earlier decisions and one decision -- 8-13 min measured on a quiet host, 42
# min with four research arms on the box; on a refit day the fit adds 10-40
# min, capped at the fit timeout init froze into that book's book.json from its
# experiment's strategy_fit_timeout_seconds (7200 s for the book in place
# today). Books run one after another.
#
# 07:40 and 08:35 are retries for a morning whose data landed late or whose
# first run was slow: flock skips a retry while an earlier run is still
# working, and a book whose session is already decided is a no-op re-render,
# never a second decision. 08:35 is the last one that still leaves the sheet in
# the operator's hands before the auction closes. The PIT event build is the
# part of the chain that can push past 05:40 under load (03:35-05:32 on a quiet
# night, 03:35-07:14 on 2026-09-16 with four arms running); a night where it
# runs past 08:35 needs the arms throttled, not another retry.
40 5 * * 1-5 cd $REPO_ROOT && mkdir -p logs/paper .runtime/paper && flock -n .runtime/paper/cron.lock $QUANT_PYTHON scripts/paper/run_paper.py run >> logs/paper/cron.log 2>&1
40 7 * * 1-5 cd $REPO_ROOT && mkdir -p logs/paper .runtime/paper && flock -n .runtime/paper/cron.lock $QUANT_PYTHON scripts/paper/run_paper.py run >> logs/paper/cron.log 2>&1
35 8 * * 1-5 cd $REPO_ROOT && mkdir -p logs/paper .runtime/paper && flock -n .runtime/paper/cron.lock $QUANT_PYTHON scripts/paper/run_paper.py run >> logs/paper/cron.log 2>&1
